# **Service Notes – AWS Bedrock + EC2 Quick Lab**  

Date: 08 Dec 2025  
Technician: Mokgadi Selepe

**Job Summary**  
Completed the AWS hands-on lab that uses Amazon Bedrock (Nova Lite model) to generate a complete static marketing webpage with a single prompt, then deployed it live on an EC2 instance running Nginx. Whole thing took under 10 minutes.

**Steps Performed**

1. Logged into AWS Console → searched for Bedrock → opened the Chat / Text playground.  
2. Selected model: Amazon → Nova Lite (On-demand).  
3. Changed settings:  
   - Max output tokens → 5120  
   - Temperature → 0 (wanted deterministic, clean code)  
4. Used this exact prompt:  
   “Generate a static webpage for AnyCompany marketing agency without any explanation.”  
5. Bedrock returned a full, valid HTML page (head, body, CSS, everything) in one shot. Copied it.  
6. Went to EC2 → found the pre-created instance named “app-server”.  
7. Grabbed the public IPv4 address and opened http://<ip> in a new tab – saw the default “Hello World” page.  
8. Connected to the instance using Session Manager (no key pair needed).  
9. Ran:  
   cd /usr/share/nginx/html  
   nano index.html  
10. Deleted the old Hello World content, pasted the AI-generated HTML, saved (Ctrl+X → Y → Enter).  
11. Refreshed the browser tab – new 100% new marketing page is now live on the EC2 public IP.

**Files Saved Locally / Pushed to GitHub**  
- index.html → exact code generated by Nova Lite  
- screenshot.png → picture of the final live page

**Observations**  
- Nova Lite with temperature 0 gives perfectly clean, ready-to-use HTML/CSS on the first try.  
- No manual coding required at all – just one prompt.  
- Session Manager makes updating files super easy, no SSH keys or security group changes.  
- Whole deploy cycle from idea to live site was literally a few minutes.

**Result**  
Customer (or anyone) can now visit the EC2 public IP and see a professional-looking marketing landing page that was 100% created by AI and deployed in seconds.

Done. Ready for next task.
